    "summary": "The exact RC26 task reached the private Redshift endpoint, authenticated as the exact Fargate task role, and set application_name=dander within one second. No user SQL appeared in SYS_QUERY_HISTORY; the Python driver then waited during connection startup until the 300-second socket timeout. This disproves the earlier cold-wake and VPC-reachability hypotheses and isolates a live candidate defect after authentication but before the first query. The provider record does not expose the missing startup message, so the lower-level driver-versus-service cause remains unproven."
